# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: collect-release-artefact-exceeds-gitlab-size-limit -- collect:release cannot upload a ~1.07 GB set (413)
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: ci-infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-07

* Symptom

The release-2.3.0 tag pipeline (2922308871): collect:release (job 17000128365)
assembled the whole release set -- 15 assets, every platform including the
GitHub-built Windows zips, manifest-release-assets.txt written -- and then
failed at the artefact upload:

#+begin_example
dist/combined/: found 17 matching artifact files and directories
ERROR: Uploading artifacts as "archive" to coordinator... 413 Payload Too Large
FATAL: too large
#+end_example

The set is ~1.07 GB: the two all-platform unions alone are 600 MB
(=clautolisp-2.3.0-all.tar.bz2= 283 MB, =clautolisp-2.3.0-all.zip= 320 MB),
duplicating every per-platform archive beside them. release-2.2.1 was under the
limit; the set grew with the macOS and arm64 binaries and the compiler.

Both publishing scripts read that artefact, so the release could not be
published by the documented procedure.

* Workaround (used for release-2.3.0, now scripted)

Collect locally on poseidon and publish from the local set:
=deploy-release-to-poseidon.sh --from DIR= and =make-gitlab-release.py
--manifest FILE --links poseidon= (AGENTS.md, release runbook). The published
links are poseidon's, so nothing depends on the GitLab artefact.

* Fix options (to decide)

1. Do not upload the =all.*= unions as the artefact: upload the per-platform
   archives + the manifest (~470 MB), and build the unions where they are
   mirrored (deploy-release-to-poseidon.sh runs =make collect-artefacts=, or a
   union step, on poseidon).
2. Drop one of the two unions (=all.zip= exists only "for Windows" and repeats
   =all.tar.bz2=), halving them.
3. Have the pipeline mirror to poseidon itself (a poseidon-tagged job with the
   web-tree access), so the combined set never has to be a GitLab artefact.

=check-release-lane-integrity= / =check-release-artefact-set= must keep
holding whichever is chosen.

* Acceptance

- A release tag pipeline's collect:release succeeds for a set of the 2.3.0
  size, and the documented procedure (deploy, then publish) works unchanged.
